-- title:
--   Universal property of the descended formal quotient tower
-- statement:
--   The statement is an existence-and-uniqueness assertion about a descended quotient map, formulated over a long list of data which fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Base ring data.** A prime $r$; a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi\in\mathcal O$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, the condition $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and the condition $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (so $\mathcal O$ is absolutely unramified with residue field of cardinality $r$); and a field $K_0$ of characteristic zero which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficient ring.** A commutative domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of characteristic zero, an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$ of it, such that: $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`); that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`); every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`); every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`); and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`), i.e. $\mathrm{Fr}$ is a Frobenius lift. Throughout, $\mathcal O_2:=$ `AlgHom.equalizer` of $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity, the subalgebra of $\mathrm{Fr}^2$-fixed elements, and $\mathcal O_{2,n}:=\mathcal O_2/(\pi^{n+1})$.
--
--   **Valuation of the determinant.** A monoid homomorphism $v_{\det}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) such that $v_{\det}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, a subgroup $\Gamma\le G$, the existence of $z\in\Gamma$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c\cdot 1$ and $v_{\det}(\sigma z)=2$ (`hcent`), the existence of $w\in\Gamma$ with $v_{\det}(\sigma w)=1$ (`hodd`), and a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by: $x\in\Gamma'$ iff $x\in\Gamma$ and $v_{\det}(\sigma x)$ is even (`hΓ'`). Further, a homomorphism $\rho:G\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with $\rho g$ the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`), the discreteness hypothesis that every vertex of the lattice tree [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) (homothety classes of full lattices) has finite stabiliser in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hdisc`), and the cocompactness hypothesis that some finite set $S$ of vertices meets every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit (`hcocpt`). An element $g_1\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed to be the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`). Finally a subgroup $N\le\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with $N\le\rho(\Gamma')$, with $N\cap\rho(\Gamma)$ normal in $\rho(\Gamma)$, and with nonzero relative index of $N$ in $\rho(\Gamma')$.
--
--   **The Mumford tower.** A term `DM : MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`; its fields (summarised here) provide schemes $Z_n$ with structure morphisms $z_{b,n}:Z_n\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ which are proper and flat, tower maps $z_{t,n}:Z_n\to Z_{n+1}$ making each square with the reduction maps a pullback, affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, a family of morphisms $q_n(B,P):\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to Z_n$ for $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (an object of `Omega K₀ π`: for each full lattice $M\subset K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule of the base change of $M$ with invertible quotient, compatible with inclusions of lattices and with homotheties, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$), subject to laws expressing that $q_n$ lies over $\mathcal O$, is natural in $B$, is compatible with $z_{t,n}$ and is invariant under pullback of Deligne data along elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ whose class lies in $N$, together with open-immersion properties of the charts.
--
--   **The covering tower and its extra structure.** Schemes $X_n$ with morphisms $x_{b,n}:X_n\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ and $x_{t,n}:X_n\to X_{n+1}$; a finite group $G_2$ acting by automorphisms $a_n:G_2\to\mathrm{Aut}(X_n)$; projections $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}:X_n\to Z_n$ and $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}:X_n\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O_{2,n}$; a homomorphism $\theta:\Gamma\to G_2$; and $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of $\mathcal O_{2,n}$. These are subject to: `hcart`, the tower squares for $(x_{t,n},x_{b,n})$ are pullbacks along the reduction maps; `hproper` and `hflat`, each $x_{b,n}$ is proper and flat; `haff`, every finite subset of $X_n$ lies in an affine open; `ha_over` and `ha_xt`, the $G_2$-action is over the base and commutes with the tower maps; `hX`, each $X_n$ is the fibre product of $Z_n$ and $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O_{2,n}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, via $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n},\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$; `hxb`, $x_{b,n}=\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ followed by $z_{b,n}$; `hxt₁` and `hxt₂`, compatibility of $x_{t,n}$ with the two projections and the corresponding tower maps; `hθsurj`, $\theta$ is surjective; `hθker`, $\theta\gamma=1$ iff $\rho\gamma\in N$; `hFr₂`, $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ sends the class of $y\in\mathcal O_2$ to the class of $\mathrm{Fr}(y)$ whenever the latter again lies in $\mathcal O_2$; `ha_pr₂`, for $\gamma\in\Gamma$ the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ equals $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ followed by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}^{-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)}$; and `ha_pr₁`, for $\gamma\in\Gamma$, $B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi^{n+1}=0$, Deligne data $P,P'$ over $B$ related by `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` for $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ (i.e. the lines of $P'$ are the preimages of the lines of $P$ under the base-changed action), and $x:\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to X_n$ with $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equal to $q_n(B,P)$, the morphism $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equals $q_n(B,P')$.
--
--   **The quotient tower and the descended quotient map.** A term `DQ : TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`, whose fields (summarised here) give schemes $Y_n$ with proper flat structure morphisms $y_{b,n}$ to $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, tower maps $y_{t,n}$ forming pullback squares with the reductions, and morphisms $p_n:X_n\to Y_n$ over the base, compatible with the tower maps, forming pullback squares, invariant under the $G_2$-action, finite and surjective, locally epimorphic, and satisfying a local universal property. In addition a family
--   $$q_n(B,(\psi,P)):\mathrm{Spec}\,B\longrightarrow Y_n$$
--   is given for each $n$, each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $B$, and each pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ and a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$ (that is, each point of `AlgFunctor.prod (AlgFunctor.corep Onr) (Omega K₀ π)` at $B$), subject to: `hqdef`, if $\psi_2:\mathcal O_{2,n}\to B$ agrees with $\psi$ on classes of elements of $\mathcal O_2$ and $x:\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to X_n$ satisfies $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equal to $q_n(B,P)$ and $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ equal to $\mathrm{Spec}\,\psi_2$, then $q_n(B,(\psi,P))$ is $x$ followed by $p_n$; `hqover`, $q_n(B,x)$ followed by $y_{b,n}$ and by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ is the structural morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$; `hqnat`, naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; `hqyt`, compatibility with $y_{t,n}$; and `hqinv`, invariance under the twisted $\Gamma$-action: for $\gamma\in\Gamma$ and points $x,x'$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (σ γ) x x'`, meaning that the first component of $x'$ is the twist `frobTwist Onr Fr` of the first component of $x$ with exponent $-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)$ and the second components are related by `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` for $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, one has $q_n(B,x')=q_n(B,x)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above, for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t:T\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$, and every family
--   $$\rho'_B:\{(\psi,P)\}\longrightarrow \{\,\varphi:\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to T \;\mid\; \varphi \text{ followed by } t \text{ is the structural morphism }\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O\,\}$$
--   defined for all $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent (the right-hand side being the value at $B$ of `Scheme.nilpPoints t`), such that $\rho'$ is natural in $B$ (the value at an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\phi:B\to B'$ of the transported point equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\phi$ followed by $\rho'_B$) and $\rho'$ is invariant under the twisted action of $\Gamma$ (for $\gamma\in\Gamma$ and $x,x'$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (σ γ) x x'`, one has $\rho'_B(x')=\rho'_B(x)$), there exists a family of morphisms $u_n:Y_n\to T$ with the following four properties:
--
--   1. for every $n$, $u_n$ followed by $t$ equals $y_{b,n}$ followed by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$;
--
--   2. for every $n$, $y_{t,n}$ followed by $u_{n+1}$ equals $u_n$;
--
--   3. for every $n$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $B$ and every point $x=(\psi,P)$ at $B$, the morphism $q_n(B,x)$ followed by $u_n$ equals the underlying morphism of $\rho'_B(x)$ (the nilpotence witness being $\pi^{n+1}=0$);
--
--   4. any family $u'_n:Y_n\to T$ satisfying the same three conditions 1–3 coincides with $u$.
--
--   Thus $u$ is the unique compatible system of morphisms over $\mathcal O$ through which the twisted-invariant natural family $\rho'$ factors via the descended quotient maps $q_n$.
--
--   This is the universal property (corepresentability statement) of the descended formal quotient in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: the tower $(Y_n)$ obtained by dividing the Mumford tower twisted by the unramified coefficients $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ by the action of $\Gamma$ receives, uniquely, any natural family of $T$-points that is invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action. It is used in the assembly of the formal quotient datum, [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum), which packages the quotient tower together with its moduli interpretation.
